<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-CN">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>如何看待线上教育?</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .title {
            background-color: #ffff00;
            font-size: 24px;
            font-weight: bold;
            padding: 5px 10px;
            display: inline-block;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .section-header {
            background-color: #d3d3d3;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 18px;
            padding: 5px 10px;
            margin-top: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .bullet-list {
            list-style-type: circle;
            margin-left: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .bullet-list li {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .red-text {
            color: #cc0000;
        }

        .blue-text {
            color: #0066cc;
        }

        .highlight-red {
            color: #cc0000;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="title">如何看待线上教育?</div>

    <div class="section-header">Introduction 开头</div>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>
            <span class="red-text">The pandemic is ranging across the globe, and students are reeling from it.</span><br>
            <span class="blue-text">(背景)</span> During the lockdown, students have no other choice but to study from home, making online education more popular. 
            <span class="blue-text">(引出话题)</span> In my view, it has both pros and cons, and should be used wisely. 
            <span class="blue-text">(抛出观点)</span>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-header">Pros 好处</div>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>
            For students, online education is more flexible. <span class="highlight-red">Rather than being restricted in classrooms</span>, leaners can sign up for any course they are interested in as long as they have the access to the Internet. 
            <span class="blue-text">(对于学生，课程选择更加灵活)</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            For teachers, they don't need to make the <span class="highlight-red">roll call</span>, because the system can record automatically. Besides, they can also assign, collect and review the homework more conveniently. 
            <span class="blue-text">(对于老师，教学更加便捷)</span>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-header">Cons 不足</div>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>
            Online courses may be effective for <span class="highlight-red">self-directed</span> learners, but students who are not organized and in possession of good time-management skills may struggle. 
            <span class="blue-text">(对于自驱型学习者有效，反之，效果不佳)</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            Online education is lacking in teacher-student interaction. It's more difficult for teachers to ask feedbacks from students. And students also can't ask questions immediately. 
            <span class="blue-text">(师生间缺少互动)</span>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-header">Conclusion 结论</div>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
        <li>
            Therefore, students should ask themselves whether they are capable of learning independently before signing up for online coursework. 
            <span class="blue-text">(所以在参与线上课程之前，学生首先应该对自己的自主学习能力有所判断)</span>
        </li>
    </ul>
</body>
</html>
```
